  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "9c35abae1178",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "73d8f9493d12",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "TL;DR:"
        },
        {
          "_key": "762fafdecba3",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Granola's native Notion integration and Zapier connector let you push structured meeting data directly into a Notion database, available on the Business plan at $14/user/month. Instead of hunting through flat documents for what a customer said three months ago, you query a tagged, filterable research repository. Adding Zapier Professional ($19.99/month billed annually) automates the entire transfer. The payoff: every customer interview becomes a citable database entry your whole team can search, not a private document that disappears when someone leaves.\n"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "blockquote"
    },
    {
      "_key": "3004328bdd39",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "814a02ab7a93",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Research insights don't die during the interview. They die afterward, buried in a document titled \"Customer Call - March\" that nobody opens again. Running multiple customer interviews each week creates a compounding retrieval problem. Each conversation captures real customer language, unfiltered reactions, and patterns that shape good product decisions. But when those conversations live in flat documents, the only way to find something specific is to remember exactly where you filed it and when. Most research debt is not a capture problem. It's a retrieval problem."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "cbdfd536df6e",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "7a0b66914a02",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Granola is the input layer: it captures high-fidelity notes without sending a visible participant into the conversation. Notion is the storage and action layer: it tags, filters, and connects those notes to roadmap items. Together, they turn scattered conversations into a queryable engine for product decisions."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "02816a0e6691",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "35b18c1131ca",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Why meeting notes die in docs but live in databases"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "29350a764d65",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "160608eb3774",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A flat document is a graveyard for context. You write the notes, close the tab, and the insight is effectively gone unless you happen to remember what you called the file. A Notion database works differently because every entry carries structured properties: date, customer segment, sentiment, feature tags, and a direct link back to the full Granola note. When a stakeholder asks \"How many customers mentioned this?\" a flat document forces you to manually scan everything. A database lets you filter by \"Feature Tag\" in seconds and return a count with sources. Research stored in personal notes also walks out the door when someone leaves. A database belongs to the organization."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "a110746f92fc",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bf522482226f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Two properties make the biggest difference:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "187e20d9b832",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "53d75e70969b",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Customer segment:"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fbcc3bda7f11",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Filter feedback by company size or plan tier to show stakeholders that multiple enterprise customers raised the same concern, not one anecdotal data point."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "9a47477b4f89",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0b5afcc1a8a7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Feature tags:"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fff91e917236",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Connect conversations to roadmap items so you can pull all relevant feedback during prioritization discussions."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "6a9ca7a210df",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "69241f216c0e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Granola captures and structures the conversation. Notion is where the work moves forward."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "da5c432c108c",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "f144b6faf04f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Setting up the Granola to Notion workflow"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "8903dce2b93d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "c4f355fb4c4f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Granola offers two paths for getting notes into Notion: a "
        },
        {
          "_key": "2e8fde8b75c2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "a55fa8355d0a"
          ],
          "text": "native Notion integration"
        },
        {
          "_key": "2952b45f2ded",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " built directly into the app, and a "
        },
        {
          "_key": "92beb3fda05a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "63ea98c65560"
          ],
          "text": "Zapier connector"
        },
        {
          "_key": "678b700f95b7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " for teams that want automated folder-based triggers and more complex routing. Both require a Business plan or above."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "a55fa8355d0a",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://help.granola.ai/article/notion"
        },
        {
          "_key": "63ea98c65560",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://help.granola.ai/article/zapier"
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "d850e56373d5",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "8c83c36e7467",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 1: Preparing your Notion database for research"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "ad57b5a727d4",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "c60198a500fb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Build the database before connecting anything. The schema below captures the essential properties for research retrieval:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "html0",
      "_type": "rawHtml",
      "html": "<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 15%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 65%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Property</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Interview date</td>\n<td>Date</td>\n<td>Filter by time period</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Participant name</td>\n<td>Text</td>\n<td>Find all feedback from one customer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Company</td>\n<td>Text</td>\n<td>Filter by account or segment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Customer segment</td>\n<td>Select</td>\n<td>Enterprise / Mid-market / SMB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Feature tags</td>\n<td>Multi-select</td>\n<td>Connect to roadmap items</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sentiment</td>\n<td>Select</td>\n<td>Positive / Neutral / Negative / Mixed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Granola link</td>\n<td>URL</td>\n<td>Direct link back to full notes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Summary</td>\n<td>Text</td>\n<td>Auto-fill from Granola's summary output</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Key themes</td>\n<td>Text</td>\n<td>Your synthesis layer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Status</td>\n<td>Select</td>\n<td>Raw / Synthesized / Shared</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "_key": "18d16cfd1a0b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b72d2ba14ed8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Granola link column is the most important property in the schema. Granola doesn't store audio files at any point: audio is transcribed in real time and then deleted. The shared link gives teammates access to the enhanced notes and lets them query the transcript through Granola's chat function, which is both a privacy benefit and a compliance simplification for sensitive customer conversations."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "a8df952e5f90",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "4d734f0a8706",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 2: Mapping Granola fields to Notion properties"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "9bd49cfafbf6",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "f272c72d0866",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Granola's "
        },
        {
          "_key": "719dcbeea30c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "b1be526c01c1"
          ],
          "text": "AI-enhanced notes"
        },
        {
          "_key": "c2d063f08d82",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " produce several structured outputs that map cleanly to Notion properties:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "b1be526c01c1",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://help.granola.ai/article/ai-enhanced-notes"
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "html1",
      "_type": "rawHtml",
      "html": "<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 25%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 25%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 50%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Granola output</th>\n<th>Notion property</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Meeting title</td>\n<td>Page title (Name)</td>\n<td>Auto-mapped in most Zap setups</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Meeting date</td>\n<td>Interview date</td>\n<td>Maps directly to date property</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Participants / Attendees</td>\n<td>Participant name</td>\n<td>May need parsing for primary interviewee</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Summary</td>\n<td>Summary text or page content</td>\n<td>{\"Map to body via \\\"Add Block to Page\\\" for longer summaries\"}</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Action items</td>\n<td>Key themes or body content</td>\n<td>Surfaces commitments clearly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Granola share link</td>\n<td>Granola link (URL)</td>\n<td>Preserves transcript access for teammates</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "_key": "de5340baf693",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "59d1eb075538",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "One practical constraint: Notion text properties cap at 2,000 characters, so longer summaries may truncate if you map them to a property field. Mapping the summary to the page content body instead, using Zapier's \"Add Block to Page\" action, avoids truncation and produces richer entries. The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "179ba820800f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "4ddc984780ff"
          ],
          "text": "Granola-Notion Zapier integration"
        },
        {
          "_key": "912a04558e30",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " supports both \"Create database item\" and \"Add Block to Page\" actions, so you can chain them in a single Zap for complete entries."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "4ddc984780ff",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://zapier.com/apps/granola/integrations/notion"
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "116679b38724",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "3b186eef5dfc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 3: Automating the transfer"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "277da6b62c13",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "85eba07d7993",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Option A: Native Notion integration (recommended for most teams)"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "e6d12f0aea5c",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "34893ba9589c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Granola's "
        },
        {
          "_key": "8e1d3bf05993",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "55d6f6d73a95"
          ],
          "text": "native Notion integration"
        },
        {
          "_key": "1ca165bedb29",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " is the simpler starting point. Go to Granola Settings, click Integrations, select Notion, and authorize the connection through your browser. Once connected, you push individual notes to Notion directly from the note sidebar, which works well for a high-touch research workflow where you want to review each note before it lands in the database."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "55d6f6d73a95",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://docs.granola.ai/help-center/sharing/notion"
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "26d34673c2df",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9076c990b2bf",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Option B: Zapier automation (recommended for volume)"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "bc02dff4973e",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6676f1e9d098",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "b12d0c0598bf",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "f1737b6aeeb9"
          ],
          "text": "Granola Zapier integration"
        },
        {
          "_key": "a01fdeb62b15",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " offers two triggers for routing notes automatically:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "f1737b6aeeb9",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://docs.granola.ai/help-center/sharing/integrations/zapier"
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "fd59c67fcd4e",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0555e60929a4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Note Added to Granola Folder:"
        },
        {
          "_key": "e3d6d7550213",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Fires when any note lands in a designated folder. Create a \"Customer Interviews\" folder in Granola, and every note placed there auto-syncs to your Notion database without manual action."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "number",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "31010cf9d4b8",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "7c26f4c6f0a6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Note Shared to Zapier:"
        },
        {
          "_key": "1359603f9956",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Fires when you manually share a note to Zapier from the sidebar, giving you more control over which notes enter the database."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "number",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "872805f1147a",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "c1fc8edeb161",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a research workflow handling multiple interviews weekly, the folder trigger is the more practical choice. "
        },
        {
          "_key": "b70cc74104d6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "bd76c272eb67"
          ],
          "text": "Zapier's Granola automation guide"
